# Findings per linter in .golangci-debt.yml, as of the change that introduced
# this gate. verify.sh re-counts and fails when any number here goes up.
#
# These are true counts, not what golangci-lint prints by default. Its own
# summary reported 197 for this same tree, because max-issues-per-linter stops
# at 50, max-same-issues at 3, and uniq-by-line keeps one finding per line.
# With those three caps off the number is 1059. The gap is the reason the caps
# are disabled in both config files: findings were being withheld from a line
# that read like a total.
#
# Per linter rather than as a sum, because one total lets a fix pay for a new
# defect and the gate would report the wrong one half the time.
#
# Lowered again once that debt was paid down. The 52 the ripgrep integration
# brought in are gone: 21 unchecked type assertions in devcouncil/grep_test.go
# now go through helpers that name the field and its actual type instead of
# panicking with "interface conversion" and nothing else; the file and
# directory modes across dc/dcgrep and grep_test are 0600 and 0750; the three
# `err != ErrNoBinary` comparisons use errors.Is, which is what the branch's own
# wrapped errors need; and readStableArtifact reports the close it was
# discarding, which on a file cargo may be replacing under it is evidence the
# bytes just read came from a file that was moving.
#
# Four suppressions rather than fixes, each narrow and each with its reason in
# place: three writes of shell scripts the tests then exec, where no mode at or
# below 0600 can work, and dc-grep's two subprocess launches, which take the
# configured binary and one of two literals this package passes.
#
# gosec, errorlint and forcetypeassert land at or below where they stood before
# that branch merged. errcheck lands one above, and where that one is has not
# been established — the branch does not touch cmd/manvi/main.go, which holds
# 113 of the 373. nilerr is six below and always was: these numbers have never
# been an exact fingerprint of this tree, which is the argument for recording
# what is measured rather than what was expected.
#
# Raised once before, from 1047, when this branch was rebased onto the
# fuzz-sweep commits. Every one of the twelve is in a file those commits added —
# llm/adaptertest/adaptertest_test.go, devcouncil/protocolfuzz_test.go,
# dc/store/protocolfuzz_test.go — and none is in code this change touches. The
# ratchet caught the increase, which is what it is for; the provenance is
# recorded here rather than the number being edited quietly.
#
# unconvert reached 0 and has moved to .golangci.yml, which is what this file
# says should happen. Getting there was not a fix but two suppressions, and the
# reason is worth recording because it is the only per-platform entry this file
# ever had: Stat_t's field widths are per-GOOS, so devcouncil/safefs.go read as
# one unnecessary conversion on darwin and three on linux. The count in this
# file was measured on darwin alone, which meant CI on Linux would have failed
# the ratchet on a tree nobody had changed. Suppressing the two lines with the
# portability reason in place makes the number 0 on both, which is the only
# count a two-platform gate can hold anyone to.
#
# A linter that reaches 0 moves to .golangci.yml and is deleted from here.
#
# Remeasured 2026-09-22 on golangci-lint 2.13.2, which is what
# `go install @latest` resolves to. The previous numbers were taken with an
# earlier 2.x. Six linters counted more and four counted less, spread across
# the existing tree (errcheck's largest file is still cmd/manvi/main.go at
# 113, the same 113 the earlier note recorded). The ratchet caught the
# movement; this is the new measurement, not a quiet edit.
#
# staticcheck and wastedassign lowered by two each on 2026-10-09, by the change
# that gave invoke_subagent and spawn_subagents one fan-out core: each copy
# assigned maxFanout from the bounds and then overwrote it unread (SA4006 and
# wastedassign on the same line, twice). The same change split Loop.Run, which
# turned two `break`s on a cancelled context into `return true, nil` in
# closeOrBounce; nilerr now reads those as a swallowed error. They are not —
# cancellation closes the turn rather than failing it, exactly as the breaks
# did — and nilerr stays inside its recorded 12. Measured with golangci-lint
# 2.14.0, because 2.13.2 cannot read go1.27.2's export data at all.
#
# Remeasured 2026-10-09 on golangci-lint 2.14.0, now what `@latest` resolves
# to, with GOOS=darwin and GOOS=linux giving the same count for every linter.
# errcheck 419 -> 413 and forcetypeassert 69 -> 68 are lowered to what both
# platforms measure. gosec and noctx are not raised to their measured 394 and
# 26: the excess is exactly the four gosec and two noctx findings a4156f3 added
# in bootstrap/bootstrap_test.go, which is a regression to fix rather than a
# new baseline.
#
# Lowered 2026-10-10, after the ratchet failed on main at b689a82 with every
# linter but wastedassign above its count: bodyclose 19, contextcheck 37,
# errcheck 447, errorlint 71, forcetypeassert 83, gosec 429, nilerr 15, noctx
# 31, staticcheck 40. 37d641f, linted against its own DevCouncil and gusset
# pins (ad5c941c, 92c2056), reproduces this file's measurement exactly, and
# b689a82 has 124 findings more. Most came from f4553ce (the Anthropic spend
# cap), bed69fe (truncated streams), 53ab7ee (pooled stream buffers), a1b3344
# (budget reclaim), f479db6 (work.scan.gaps) and 3d3d257 (work.verify.task).
# None of them carries a verification note GitPulse can read, so nothing
# records the ratchet having run on the commits that crossed it.
#
# Every new finding was fixed or annotated where it stands. Five were defects:
# serve's devmap root check passed an envelope whose repository field could
# not be decoded; work.scan.gaps read tracked documents through symlinks out of
# the repository and looked up referenced paths that climbed out of it (it now
# reads through an os.Root); bootstrap discarded a failed removal of the check
# file it writes into the operator's tree; `manvi budget` dropped its write
# errors; and opening, reporting, reconciling the ledger and reading its
# headroom waited out a 30s lock under context.Background() whatever the
# caller had given up on. The last is why budget.Open, Snapshot, Inspect,
# ReconcileAt, agents.Budget.Headroom, buildProvider, budgetCommand,
# showLocal and probe take a context now: those signatures were the source of
# the contextcheck findings in verifycritic.go and the budget slash command.
# Recording a sent attempt keeps its caller's values but not its cancellation
# (context.WithoutCancel), because the attempt is billed either way.
#
# What was annotated instead is not a defect, and says why on the line: fixed-
# seed randomness in tests, a test re-execing its own binary, the literal git,
# strings.Builder writes, a server-lifetime lane worker, a decode whose nil is
# the success path, and mcp.Manager.Discover, which never reads its ctx (one
# annotation at each of its three ctx-holding callers; harness.go says they
# depend on that staying true).
#
# errcheck is 385 for this change on its own and 379 once the `manvi
# providers` restyle that was in flight beside it lands, because that restyle
# removes six findings from providers.go. Both were measured; 385 is recorded
# so that the order the two land in does not matter. The bootstrap_test.go
# regression noted above was fixed inside the window, which is why gosec and
# noctx no longer exceed their counts. bed69fe also left the enforced set
# failing on four ruleguard findings (an unbounded io.ReadAll three times in
# streamguard_test.go, a reasonless t.Skip in a fuzz target), which verify.sh
# would have stopped on before reaching this gate; they are fixed with the
# rest. Every number below was measured with golangci-lint 2.14.0 on
# GOOS=darwin and GOOS=linux, against DevCouncil acfaa229 and gusset 23e925b
# (scripts/module-pins.txt), and is the same on both.
bodyclose 14
contextcheck 21
errcheck 179
errorlint 1
forcetypeassert 54
# gosec is 392 on both darwin and linux after the pty ioctl unsafe.Pointer
# calls were marked #nosec G103. Before that, pty_linux_test.go had two
# findings and pty_darwin_test.go had one, so a count measured on darwin
# failed the Ubuntu job by one. Do not lower this number from a darwin-only
# recount that still includes those lines.
gosec 255
nilerr 10
noctx 21
staticcheck 33
wastedassign 5
